  "goodToKnow": "Die Violine is the violin; the everyday German word is die Geige. Die erste Geige spielen means to call the shots. Der Violinschlüssel is the treble clef. Mittenwald in Bavaria has a centuries-old violin-making (Geigenbau) tradition, and Anne-Sophie Mutter is one of the world's most famous violinists. Der Himmel hängt voller Geigen means to be blissfully happy. Plural: die Violinen."
